a3=base.replace('She watches the remaining gap as she works, lips slightly parted,','Pressed close to the doorway jamb, she looks over her shoulder into the shadowed corridor as she works, lips slightly parted,').replace('A warm portable work lamp describes her face and fingers against cold blue reflections on the transparent sheet;','A warm portable work lamp illuminates her fingers while her face remains in doorway shadow with a readable soft rim against cold blue reflections on the transparent sheet;')
for name,prompt in [('A1',a1),('A2',a2),('A3',a3)]: (p/(name+'.prompt.txt')).write_text(prompt+'\n')
comparison='''# B composition comparison

Frozen baseline: revisions/77409debcba1462cb7526227b5113da2/baseline.txt (SHA-256 ad165eeb588d3acfce10b4c37d01c4f1a526427457d75a6196200bdadd3b35a6). Creative controls remain creativity 1, sensual 1, fetish 0, surreal 0. The requested topic/reference use are invariant; the cryogenic bay, clamp, membrane, knee/boot, mechanics and photographic treatment are agent-owned. Local changes are compared at the same strengths, with no source adoption quota. Every source retains its native_approval:false boundary. Comparison prose supplies no native permission.

The baseline gives one cause/action/result route: an external tear is seen behind a clear sheet, the right hand works the last clamp, the adjacent gap carries the outgoing condensation, and the face follows that gap. Its weakness is a demanding simultaneous visibility problem, especially sheet curvature and fine stream direction. The independent test is allowed to fail on those pixels.

## A1 - explicit fear on the same working face
Source R01 (CID cand_558e8b5191d257a3b46d92366b39268b, RID base, SHA ed895b6fe866157f950a9fd5b5e57f3f16c13d951e43dbd47d676f52c8882fb2). The expression dimension is open and reference facial shape/hair stay literal. The complete tear/lip cue is represented for artistic comparison; no source adoption is selected. It strengthens personal fear and keeps the pressure event coherent, but two tiny tear menisci compete with the small seal and shift the person from practical concentration toward a prescribed fear demonstration. The baseline's parted breath and purposeful gaze suit the subtle human appeal better at this frame scale.

'''+a1+'''

## A2 - peeling boundary corner
Source R07 (CID cand_f866a65395325d37942f158e94a5a108, RID base, SHA c32c6948744c4cf31de835633ce6fd581a642abd2d5a05c04c2c9dba8a83ba05). The action/material/pose changes are open and the reference property is untouched. It retains the entire flap/front/reverse/substrate relation rather than copying only peel. It makes a physical failure more tactile, but adds adhesive delamination to an already readable incomplete clamp and gives the small corner too many surfaces. The baseline has the cleaner current action and fewer competing boundaries.

'''+a2+'''

## A3 - doorway vigilance
Source R09 (CID cand_2432545cf2005270a95d5aaff0c8492f, RID base, SHA 73d9b9d947ac2bcc43136f704539407db8fa3191e9f6fa1bac31aece6d5e65e6). Open gaze/action and lighting changes keep her near the doorway and turn attention into the corridor from shadow. The hand can continue the clamp action while she checks behind her, so this is physically possible and adds an off-frame uncertainty. Its tradeoff is a second target and weaker face-gap-clamp continuity, with the reference face harder to judge. At creativity 1 the baseline offers stronger situational clarity and a better face/hand relationship.

'''+a3+'''

## Selection
The exact frozen baseline wins. Its lower information burden and one directed attention/action line serve this pressure-boundary test better. No material candidate is retained as inspiration and no whole source is adopted. This is a preference after complete alternatives, not a claim that the baseline is defect-free or that random retrieval establishes data quality. A1/A2/A3 remain unchosen, unrendered comparisons; they add no gate or obligation.

## Candidate review
All 32 query/CID/RID occurrences were read in material-view.json and materials-complete.json, including complete native text, EN/KO meaning, conditions, and effects. The table below links every unique occurrence to a source-specific judgment; source-reviews.json and composed.input.json retain exact source hashes.

'''
for r in reviews: comparison+='- '+r['review_id']+' | '+r['query']+' | '+r['candidate_id']+'/'+r['realization_id']+' | '+r['source_sha256']+' | '+r['rationale']+'\n'
comparison+='\nSearch limitation: contact_point returned zero because its scene-context phrase "without hiding the clamp" was classified as nonpositive_scope_without_requested_change. The sealed plan was not changed or resampled. Other four queries returned eight sources each; all 32 sources were distinct. New space-horror source exposure is R27/V02 and R28/V64; both are skipped, so the image cannot be cited as evidence that those newly installed candidates were adopted. The baseline itself was independently frozen before this material access.\n'
(p/'composition-comparison.md').write_text(comparison)
